{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeuvEk9wt7EfArbZ1U8tj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the `ErrorCode` enum to represent state conflicts like attempting to confirm a cancelled shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Fetches the shipment by ID (throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - Return ResponseEntity with the (possibly unchanged) shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test cases:\n   - Confirms a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change (idempotency)\n   - Rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409 and error envelope\n   - Rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404 and error envelope\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Using ValidationException instead of ConflictException for cancelled state: Rejected because ConflictException (409) is the correct semantic for \"operation conflicts with current state\", per HTTP standards. ValidationException (400) is for malformed input, not state conflicts.\n- Adding a service layer vs direct logic in controller: Rejected because the existing codebase does logic directly in controllers (see create method in ShipmentController), so maintaining consistency is more important than adding a new layer.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Response | Code |\n|------|-------|------|-------|----------|------|\n| Create→Confirm | shipmentId=S-1, status=CREATED | find S-1 | update to CONFIRMED | 200 Shipment | success |\n| Idempotent | shipmentId=S-1, status=CONFIRMED | find S-1 | (no change) | 200 Shipment | success |\n| Cancelled reject | shipmentId=S-1, status=CANCELLED | find S-1 | (no write) | 409 error envelope | SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS |\n| Not found | shipmentId=missing | not found | (no write) | 404 error envelope | SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: Confirms a CREATED shipment** — Create shipment S-1, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED and 200 OK returned\n2. **Test: Idempotent confirm** — Create and confirm S-2, confirm again, verify status unchanged and 200 OK (no error)\n3. **Test: Reject CANCELLED shipment** — Directly save cancelled shipment, POST confirm, verify 409 with error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n4. **Test: Reject unknown shipment** — POST confirm on non-existent S-999, verify 404 with error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me start by adding the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":24859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a16736c-859e-4ab6-973c-0dbc415d3a69","uuid":"93b2774d-f7f0-41ea-a1d2-fbdb31ccba87","timestamp":"2026-09-10T14:30:16.005Z","request_id":"req_011CeuvEihPJZXkSoPoY3XKA"}
